      "authorTitle": "Qualified UGC NET DEC-2024 & 2025 for Assistant Professor & Admission to Ph.D. in Computer Science & Application",
      "contentHtml": "<p>&nbsp;Women Empowerment means to empower women to live glorious and \nrespectful life. They are the backbone of society, so their empowerment is \nempowerment of society. They work like mother, sister, daughter and wife. \nThey play major role in creation of ideal society. They bind whole family in a \nsingle unit and maintain balance in family. They sacrifice their whole life\nin welfare of their family. It is said in Sanskrit that “<b>Yatr Naryastu Pujyante \n,Ramante Tatr Devta</b>.” This means that where women is respected, God \nremains there.&nbsp;</p><p>Women consists of the 50% of the population so their development is \nthe best way to improve the condition of the society. We can never think \nabout the development of society without development of women. We must \nstart development from grass root level because they are left behind in the \nprocess of development. We must respect them so that we may get their \nblessing. Today in materialistic world we are treating women as thing and \nexploiting them. They are key stone of the society so we must protect them. They are not a thing; they have life and they are free to live a respectful life. \nMostly women are suffered from human trafficking. This is a social evil present \nin the society. They also face domestic violence in family after marriage. Now \ndays they are suffered from ignorance because their children leave them \nalone. They have needed a support in old age but their children leave them alone.\nThis evil is spreading in the world very fast if it will not be controlled then one \nday a large number of women suffered from this. This is not a social problem \nbut it has become global problem so we must think for its solution so that they \nmay be saved from this evil. They have to spend their life in old age home. They \nfeel very tired in old age, yet they have to work to survive. We must support \nthem so that they may spent their remaining time with happiness. The parents \nbear their children and look after them till they become self-dependent, but \nchildren never think for their Parents and leave them alone. We should \npromote the scheme related to women. We must ensure their participation in \ndevelopment. We encourage them so that they may live respectful life. Government has started a lot of schemes to promote women as UJWALA \nYojana, ODF scheme, Beti Bachao Beti Padhao Scheme, Sukanya Samridhi \nYojana etc.. In UJWALA Yojana government provides free LPG connection to \nwomen. This scheme benefits the women living below poverty line. Now they \nare using LPG for cooking in villages. They are living a respectable life. They \noften used firewood for cooking. This scheme helps them to live a standard life \nand to improve their life expectancy. We should protect them from violence \nand other illegal work. It is responsibility of whole society that they care for \nwomen and provide equal opportunity to grow in life.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;It is concluded that the protection of women is responsibility of man. They have need respect because they are also an inseparable part of our \nsociety and family. They teach their children high standard Sanskaras and play \nmajor role in creation of ideal society and better future of the country. Thus,\nthey must be respected. It is said that women are base of the society. So It is \nsaid that “<b>You educate a man; you educate a man. You educate a woman; you \neducate a generation.”&nbsp;</b></p><p><br /></p><p><br /></p><p><br /></p>",
